{
  "info": {
    "title": "Ozone Connect - Consent Event & Action APIs",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Ozone Financial Technology Limited"
    },
    "description": "This document provides an API description in [OpenAPI](https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.0.1.html) for APIs that are called by Ozone Connect to inform a  financial institution that a consent has been created or modified.\n\nThese are also used to carry out actions to verify and augment a consent when it is being created.\n\nThese APIs should be implemented by an financial institution.\n\nPlease refer to the API Hub documentation for details of test cases that are available for this API  using the Ozone Connect test suite.\n### Versioning\nThe `version` property implements the following pattern `{standards-major}.{standards-minor}.{ozone-connect-version}`, where:\n* `standards-major` is the major version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `standards-minor` is the minor version of the latest UAE standard that the API description implements.\n* `ozone-connect-version` is the version of the Ozone Connect API description.\n\nSo, for example, `v2.0.1` indicates the first version of the Ozone Connect API description that implements the UAE standard version 2.0.\n\n**Please adhere to the deprecated flags in your implementation. Do not implement deprecated properties when** **implementing new functionality.**\n\n**Please use the OpenAPI description document attached to the page if you reading this in Confluence** **to check for deprecated properties.**\n### v2.2.1\n* Added new version compatible with v2.2 of standards\n* Changed every date-time field to reference the shared `AEDateTime` Schema Object. `AEDateTime` states that a\n  date-time value identifies an instant, that the offset is part of the value and must be applied by the\n  recipient, and that two encodings of the same instant are equivalent and must behave identically. It carries\n  a `pattern` requiring an offset and forbidding `-00:00`; all other offsets remain conformant. Each field\n  description now states only what is specific to that field. Per OFP-014.\n\n### v2.1.7\n* Added `ReadStatements` and `ReadProductFinanceRates` to `AEAccountAccessConsentPermissionCodes`, matching the\n  same addition to the Consent Manager. Both codes are in the v2.1 Standards Bank Data Sharing permission set, so\n  the Hub can forward them on a consent event; without them a valid consent failed validation at the LFI.\n* Added a character-set `pattern` (`^[A-Za-z0-9 \\/?:().,'+-]+$`, the ISO 20022 / SWIFT \"x\" set) to the\n  current (free-text, 35-char) branch of the Creditor and Debtor references\n  (`AEServiceInitiationCreditorReference` / `AEServiceInitiationDebtorReference`), so every LFI knows\n  exactly which characters it must accept and store. The deprecated structured (120-char) branch is\n  unchanged. Per OFP-003.\n\n### v2.1.6\n* Restructured the international Creditor PII (`PersonalIdentifiableInformation.Initiation.Creditor`) for\n  SWIFT SR2026: the Creditor party is now a `oneOf` of Individual and Organization variants, discriminated\n  by `IdentityType`.\n\n\n* The Individual variant carries object-valued `FirstName` / `MiddleName` / `LastName` (`en` / `ar` / `ls`),\n  `RelationshipToSender`, `DateOfBirth`, `Occupation`, `Nationality`, `Gender`, `CountryOfBirth`,\n  `SourceOfIncome`, `SourceOfFunds`, and `Evidence`. The Organization variant carries `AnyBIC`, `LEI`, and\n  `Identification` + `SchemeName`. Both variants share `MobileNumber` / `Email` and an object-valued `Name`\n  (`en` / `ar` / `ls`).\n\n\n* Added SWIFT SR2026 fields to the international `PostalAddress` (`PostCode`, `Room`, `Department`,\n  `SubDepartment`, `TownLocationName`, and now-mandatory `TownName`). It is now a single\n  `AEInternationalAddress` schema shared by both the Creditor and the Creditor Agent (the Creditor Agent\n  previously used the legacy `AEAddress`).\n\n\n* Added a `CreditorAgent.Branch` object and `CreditorAccount.AccountType` (Savings / Current / Checking /\n  Prepaid). Domestic Creditor schemas are unchanged.\n\n\n### v2.1.5\n* Aligned the `Risk` object with Standards: updated `AEAccountTypeCode` and the inline `AEBankServiceInitiationRichAuthorizationRequests.AECreditorIndicators.AccountType` enum to `Retail / SME / Corporate` (was `Retail / Corporate` and a divergent `CurrentAccount / Savings / CreditCard / Mortgage / Finance` respectively), tightened `AERisk` and its descendants with `additionalProperties: false` on the payment-initiation side, carved out the three RAR-shape `SupplementaryData` blocks (`AEBankServiceInitiationRichAuthorizationRequests.AE*Indicators.SupplementaryData`) to be open extension points, and added `minLength: 1` / `maxLength: 70` to the `AddressLine` items.\n\n### v2.1.4\n* Changed the `Amount` schema `pattern` regex, which was over-escaped in YAML and failed to validate decimal\n  monetary values.\n\n### v2.1.3\n* Added revised PII properties compatible with version 2.1.\n\n* Changed DebtorReference and CreditorReference to reflect v2.0 properties.\n\n* Changed Rich Authorization Request `type` values to reflect exactly the consent type they are describing.\n### v2.1.2\n* Changed API description to synchronise consent Schema Objects with Consent Manager API description.\n### v2.1.1\n* Added `Type` to `CreditorAccount` in `PersonalIdentifiableInformation`.\n* Changed loan to finance for all Schema Objects names and object descriptions.\n* Changed CreditorReference and DebtorReference objects to remove pattern\n* Changed CreditorReference, DebtorReference, and Reference objects to reduce maximum length to 35 characters.\n* Removed support for single future-dated payment consents that are warehoused at the LFI.",
    "version": "v2.2.1"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://[Ozone_Connect_API]"
    }
  ],
  "source_path": "/consent/action/validate",
  "operations": {
    "post": {
      "tags": [
        "consent-actions"
      ],
      "summary": "Provides an opportunity for a financial institution to validate a consent before it is created",
      "description": "The API is called by Ozone to allow a financial institution to carry out additional validations before a consent is created.\n\nThe request body contains the entire consent along with contextual information.\n\nTypically this could be used for situations like:\n- soft validation of the debtor account (e.g. to ensure that it is a debtor account managed by the financial institution)\n- populating charges and exchange rate information\n\nNote that a financial institution only need to implement this API where it needs to correlate information in the consent payload\nwith data held in its systems. If this is not the case, \"local\" validations can be configured in Ozone that do not require a remote call.\n\nThe financial institution must return a response that includes a status. If the status is set to `valid`, the consent is saved and processing continues.\n\nIf the status is set to `invalid` the processing fails and an error response is sent to the TPP.\n",
      "operationId": "validateConsent",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/providerId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/aspspId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerOrgId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerClientId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerSoftwareStatementId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiUri"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/apiOperation"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/consentId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/callerInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ozoneInteractionId"
        },
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/parameters/psuIdentifier"
        }
      ],
      "requestBody": {
        "required": true,
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/consent"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "responses": {
        "200": {
          "description": "successful operation",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/consentValidateResponse"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "400": {
          "description": "failed operation",
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "default": {
          "$ref": "#/components/responses/Error"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "security": [
    {},
    {
      "OzoneConnectApiKey": []
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": [
        "placeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "securitySchemes": {
    "OzoneConnectApiKey": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using an API Key, which is a secret shared between the API Hub and the LFI.",
      "type": "apiKey",
      "in": "header",
      "name": "Authorization"
    },
    "OzoneConnectClientCredentials": {
      "type": "oauth2",
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using a Client Credentials grant type.\n\nLFIs must host an OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server to utilise this security pattern. Scope values are set during the onboarding process, and represented by a placeholder in this API description.\n",
      "flows": {
        "clientCredentials": {
          "tokenUrl": "https://example.lfi.ae/token",
          "scopes": {
            "placeholder": "Placeholder for scopes, which are set by the LFI during onboarding"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "OzoneConnectJwtAuth": {
      "description": "Communications between the API Hub and the LFI Ozone Connect implementation are secured using the \"JWT Auth\" mechanism, where the Client presents a signed JSON Web Token as a credential.\n\nThe Server MUST verify the signature in order to authenticate the Client.\n\nPlease note that the value of the `scheme` parameter is not a registered HTTP Authentication Scheme, to indicate it is specific to Ozone Connect. Please refer to API Hub documentation for further details.\n",
      "type": "http",
      "scheme": "Ozone-Connect-JWT-Auth"
    }
  }
}

{
  "name": "o3-provider-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "Identifier for the financial institution that the request is targetted to"
}

{
  "name": "o3-aspsp-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "deprecated": true,
  "description": "Identifier for the financial institution that the request is targetted to. This header is deprecated and will be removed in a future version of Ozone Connect. Use `o3-provider-id` instead."
}

{
  "name": "o3-caller-org-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "An identifier for the organization calling the API"
}

{
  "name": "o3-caller-client-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "An identifier for the OIDC clientId calling the API"
}

{
  "name": "o3-caller-software-statement-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "An identifier for the software statement calling the API"
}

{
  "name": "o3-api-uri",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "The parameterised URL of the API being called by the caller"
}

{
  "name": "o3-api-operation",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "The API operation carried out by the caller (e.g. GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH)"
}

{
  "name": "o3-consent-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "The consentId for which this call is being made"
}

{
  "name": "o3-caller-interaction-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": false,
  "description": "The interaction ID passed in by the caller, if any"
}

{
  "name": "o3-ozone-interaction-id",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": true,
  "description": "An interaction ID generated by Ozone if the caller did not send in one. If the callerInteractionId is specified, this takes the same value."
}

{
  "name": "o3-psu-identifier",
  "in": "header",
  "schema": {
    "type": "string"
  },
  "required": false,
  "description": "A Base64 encoded representation of the psuIdentifier JSON object."
}

{
  "description": "\nA consent in its current state.\n\nIf the consent has been authorised, then it can be expected that the financial institution would have patched in `accountIds` and `psuIdentifier` fields.\n\nAdditionally, the financial institution may also patch in an arbitrary set of fields along with consent in the `supplementaryInformation` field.\n",
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/newConsent"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConsentManager.AEUpdatedConsentProperties"
    },
    {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "authorizationChannel": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "App",
            "Web"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A unique identifier for the consent in uuid-v4 format.\n"
    },
    "parId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A unique identifier for the PAR request that created this consent.\nThe value matches the value of the request_uri returned by the post call to the PAR endpoint.\n"
    },
    "rarType": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^urn:openfinanceuae:(?:account-access|insurance|service-initiation)-consent:v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$",
      "description": "The authorization detail type of the RAR request that resulted in this consent.\nThis value matches the Type of the authorization_details element of the RAR request.\nIts value will be one of the authorization_details_types_supported on the well-known endpoint.\n"
    },
    "standardVersion": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The standardVersion field specifies the standardized version of an API set. An API set refers to a group of APIs designed to deliver a specific functionality (e.g., accounts, payments, insurance). Example values: 'v1.0', 'v2.1', or 'insurance:v1.1'.\"\n"
    },
    "consentGroupId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A unique identifier for the consent group in uuid-v4 format.\nThe consent group id is used to group together consents that are related to each other.\n"
    },
    "requestUrl": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "uri",
      "description": "The request url of Http request that was received by Ozone from the TPP\n"
    },
    "consentType": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The type of the consent that is being created.\n\nEach financial institution's instance may support a different set of consent types\nThe Consent Manager supports the creation of consents of different consent types depending on the standards supported.\n\n- cbuae-account-access-consents\n- cbuae-service-initiation-consents\n- cbuae-insurance-consents\n"
    },
    "status": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEConsentStatus"
    },
    "request": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AuthorizationDetails"
    },
    "requestHeaders": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "The entire set of Http request headers that was received by Ozone from the TPP\n"
    },
    "consentBody": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/cbuaeConsentBody"
    },
    "interactionId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The Heimdall `interactionId` that this consent is associated with."
    },
    "tpp": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/tpp"
    },
    "ozoneSupplementaryInformation": {
      "type": "object"
    },
    "updatedAt": {
      "description": "When the consent was last updated, as an epoch-based date/time",
      "type": "number"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "consentType",
    "consentBody",
    "request",
    "requestHeaders",
    "tpp"
  ]
}

{
  "description": "The request body for creating a new consent.\n\nThe body consists of the RAR request that is sent by the TPP to the authorization server.\n",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DataSharingAuthorizationDetails"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InsuranceAuthorizationDetails"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ServiceInitiationAuthorizationDetails"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "type": {
      "description": "The Rich Authorization Request (RAR) type",
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^urn:openfinanceuae:account-access-consent:v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$",
      "example": "urn:openfinanceuae:account-access-consent:v2.2"
    },
    "consent": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AuthorizationDetailsDataSharingConsent"
    },
    "subscription": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EventNotification"
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "ConsentId",
    "Permissions",
    "OpenFinanceBilling",
    "ExpirationDateTime"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "ConsentId": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEConsentId"
    },
    "Permissions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAccountAccessConsentPermissionCodes"
      },
      "minItems": 1
    },
    "OpenFinanceBilling": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAccountAccessOpenFinanceBillingPost"
    }
  },
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAccountAccessAuthorizationDetailsProperties"
    }
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}

{
  "type": "string",
  "minLength": 1,
  "maxLength": 128,
  "description": "Unique identification assigned by the TPP to identify the consent resource."
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "UserType",
    "Purpose"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "UserType": {
      "description": "Type of Customer",
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "Retail",
        "SME",
        "Corporate"
      ]
    },
    "Purpose": {
      "description": "Purpose of data sharing request",
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "AccountAggregation",
        "RiskAssessment",
        "TaxFiling",
        "Onboarding",
        "Verification",
        "QuoteComparison",
        "BudgetingAnalysis",
        "FinancialAdvice",
        "AuditReconciliation"
      ]
    }
  },
  "description": "Billing parameters specified by the TPP",
  "additionalProperties": false
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "BaseConsentId": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEBaseConsentId"
    },
    "AuthorizationExpirationDateTime": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAuthorizationExpirationDateTime"
    },
    "ExpirationDateTime": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEDateTime"
        },
        {
          "description": "Specified date and time the permissions will expire."
        }
      ]
    },
    "TransactionFromDateTime": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEDateTime"
        },
        {
          "description": "Specified start date and time for the transaction query period.\n\nIf this is not populated, the start date will be open ended, and\ndata will be returned from the earliest available\ntransaction.\n\n**DEPRECATED AT V2.1, REPLACED BY `FromDate`**"
        }
      ]
    },
    "TransactionToDateTime": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEDateTime"
        },
        {
          "description": "Specified end date and time for the transaction query period.\n\nIf this is not populated, the end date will be open ended, and\ndata will be returned to the latest available transaction.\n\n**DEPRECATED AT V2.1, REPLACED BY `ToDate`**"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FromDate": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEBankDataSharingRichAuthorizationRequests.AEBankDataSharingFromDate"
    },
    "ToDate": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEBankDataSharingRichAuthorizationRequests.AEBankDataSharingToDate"
    },
    "AccountType": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEExternalAccountTypeCode"
      }
    },
    "AccountSubType": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAccountSubTypeCode"
      }
    },
    "OnBehalfOf": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEOnBehalfOf"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}

{
  "type": "string",
  "minLength": 1,
  "maxLength": 128,
  "description": "The original ConsentId assigned by the TPP"
}

{
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEDateTime"
    },
    {
      "description": "The date and time by which a Consent (in AwaitingAuthorization status) must be Authorized by the User."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "type": "string",
  "format": "date",
  "description": "Specified start date for the transaction or statement query period.\n\nIf this is not populated, the start date will be open ended, and data will be returned from the earliest available transaction or statement.\n\nAll dates in the JSON payloads are represented in ISO 8601 date format.  For example: 2025-01-01"
}

{
  "type": "string",
  "format": "date",
  "description": "Specified end date for the transaction or statement query period.\n\nIf this is not populated, the end date will be open ended, and data will be returned to the latest available transaction or the last statement generated.\n\nAll dates in the JSON payloads are represented in ISO 8601 date format.  For example: 2025-12-31"
}

{
  "description": "Specifies the type of account (Retail, SME or Corporate).",
  "type": "string",
  "enum": [
    "Retail",
    "SME",
    "Corporate"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "TradingName": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Trading Name"
    },
    "LegalName": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Legal Name"
    },
    "IdentifierType": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEOnBehalfOfIdentifierType"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Identifier Type"
    },
    "Identifier": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}

{
  "type": "string",
  "enum": [
    "Other"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "description": "A Webhook Subscription Schema\n",
  "required": [
    "Webhook"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "Webhook": {
      "description": "A Webhook Schema\n",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "Url",
        "IsActive"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "Url": {
          "description": "The TPP Callback URL being registered with the LFI\n",
          "type": "string",
          "example": "https://api.tpp.com/webhook/callbackUrl"
        },
        "IsActive": {
          "description": "The TPP specifying whether the LFI should send (IsActive true) or not send (IsActive false) Webhook Notifications to the TPP's Webhook URL\n",
          "type": "boolean",
          "example": false
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "type": {
      "description": "The Rich Authorization Request (RAR) type",
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^urn:openfinanceuae:insurance-consent:v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$",
      "example": "urn:openfinanceuae:insurance-consent:v2.2"
    },
    "consent": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AuthorizationDetailsInsuranceConsent"
    },
    "subscription": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EventNotification"
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "ConsentId",
    "Permissions",
    "OpenFinanceBilling",
    "ExpirationDateTime"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "BaseConsentId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The original ConsentId assigned by the TPP"
    },
    "AuthorizationExpirationDateTime": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEAuthorizationExpirationDateTime"
    },
    "ExpirationDateTime": {
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEDateTime"
        },
        {
          "description": "Specified date and time the permissions will expire."
        }
      ]
    },
    "OnBehalfOf": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OnBehalfOf"
    },
    "ConsentId": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEConsentId"
    },
    "Permissions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEInsuranceConsentPermissions"
      },
      "minItems": 1
    },
    "OpenFinanceBilling": {
      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AEInsuranceOpenFinanceBillingPost"
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "description": "On Behalf Of",
